WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:07.060
Gregor Mendel’s experiments were a breakthrough

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.280
in the field of Biology as they helped in

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.600
laying the foundation of Genetics.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.440
Questions like “Why do kids look similar

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.980
to their parents” and “Why are there a

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.840
few differences in 2 kids that belong to the

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.700
same parents?” started gaining answers.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.640
We now have understood the Monohybrid cross

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.340
and the monohybrid ratio as well.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.080
This is how it is done!

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.870
Take a moment to review it!

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.149
How did we get the F one generation?

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:42.366
We got it by considering all the possible

00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:43.340
combinations here.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:48.000
But is there a method to find it systematically?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.630
Yes!

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.304
So before moving ahead with the Dihybrid cross

00:00:52.304 --> 00:00:54.920
and ratio, let us have a look at an extremely

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.519
important and useful method for writing a cross.

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:03.106
The method is named as Punnett square ! You

00:01:03.106 --> 00:01:06.610
may wonder why we need one more method for

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.359
a theoretical cross, when we already know

00:01:09.359 --> 00:01:11.170
how a cross is carried out…

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.840
Well, that is because this method is quite

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.860
useful in many ways.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.120
The technique was developed by the British

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.040
geneticist Reginald Punnett . Hence it is

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.530
most commonly known as Punnett square.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:31.180
Let us understand the technique step by step first.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.070
The first thing we do is, make a table like this!

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:38.060
We write the symbols of male and female here.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.260
These can be written vice versa as well, but

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.700
for now we write it like this!

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.238
This tells us that the maternal alleles will

00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:49.660
be written here while the paternal alleles

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:52.140
will be written here.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.500
So let us begin the crossing now!

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.993
This allele can come together with this one

00:01:56.993 --> 00:01:59.660
to give us this set of genes in the offspring.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.130
These two can give us this set.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.840
This one will combine with this to give us this set.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.330
And what about the last one?

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.330
Yes!

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.170
You guessed it right!

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:14.030
These two alleles can give us this set in the offspring.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:17.507
It’s a simple concept of respective row

00:02:17.507 --> 00:02:20.450
and column pairing for each slot.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.300
For this slot, it’s the first row and the first column.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.680
For this slot, it’s the first row and the

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.420
second column pairing… and so on!

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.820
Please understand this well because it is

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.500
going to help us a lot in the future!

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.029
Now, if we compare the simple cross that we

00:02:38.029 --> 00:02:41.220
usually carry out, this is what we get.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.710
Notice that the results are exactly the same.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:48.372
All the plants in the F1 generation are tall,

00:02:48.372 --> 00:02:50.569
and have the same genotype.

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:53.310
They are all heterozygous!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.400
This confirms that our cross is correct!

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.486
A glance at the presentation of this cross

00:03:00.486 --> 00:03:02.690
hints at one more name for it!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:03.690
Yes!

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.084
This technique is also referred to as the

00:03:06.084 --> 00:03:07.310
checkerboard method .

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.631
Now, let us do this cross one more time to

00:03:10.631 --> 00:03:14.190
know whether we have understood it correctly!

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:18.410
Let us cross any two from the F1 generation now.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.646
Again, we first draw these lines to form a

00:03:21.646 --> 00:03:24.959
table and write the male and female symbols

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:26.280
here.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.569
Now it’s the turn of the genes.

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:32.520
So we write the respective genes here and here.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.260
Shall we begin crossing now?

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.350
Why don’t you try filling in these 4 slots?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.930
Here we go!

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.328
These are the combinations that we obtain

00:03:43.328 --> 00:03:45.400
on crossing these plants.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.450
Take a moment to go through this table.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.720
Can you find the phenotypic and genotypic

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.160
ratios here?

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.819
Phenotype if you remember, refers to observable

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:00.230
physical properties.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.940
We can clearly see that there are three tall

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.460
plants and one dwarf plant.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:09.420
So the phenotypic ratio is three to one!

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.490
What about the genotype?

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:15.260
There is one homozygous tall case, two heterozygous

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:19.340
tall cases, and one homozygous recessive case!

00:04:19.349 --> 00:04:23.430
So the genotypic ratio is one to two to one!

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.729
Aren’t these the monohybrid ratios?

00:04:25.729 --> 00:04:26.729
Yes!

00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:30.909
We get exactly the same results that we obtained

00:04:30.909 --> 00:04:34.479
on crossing the F1 generation previously.

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:38.608
So, this is how monohybrid cross can be carried

00:04:38.608 --> 00:04:41.770
out using the Punnett square method.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:44.566
Can you guess why this method is used when

00:04:44.566 --> 00:04:46.830
we can cross the alleles directly?

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.698
Yes, of course we can find it directly…

00:04:49.698 --> 00:04:53.080
but that’s because a monohybrid cross involves

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.270
the crossing of a single character at a time!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.750
Hence it’s easy!

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:01.104
But what about the crosses that involve more

00:05:01.104 --> 00:05:02.120
than one character?

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.054
An increase in the number of genes can make

00:05:05.054 --> 00:05:07.169
the crossing a bit complicated.

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:10.180
Say we have two or three genes.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.100
Then do you think a simple cross like this

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.800
will be convenient to carry out?

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.340
Of course not!

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:19.559
It will be a huge mess!

00:05:19.559 --> 00:05:22.262
So in order to simplify this, we make use

00:05:22.262 --> 00:05:23.580
of a Punnett square.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.221
This method is simple and extremely useful

00:05:27.221 --> 00:05:30.689
when more than one alleles are involved!

00:05:30.689 --> 00:05:33.129
Talking about crosses involving more than

00:05:33.129 --> 00:05:35.569
one character, what are crosses involving

00:05:35.569 --> 00:05:37.340
2 characters called?

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.576
The cross involving two characters at a time

00:05:40.576 --> 00:05:44.180
is called a Dihybrid cross and the ratio obtained

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.159
will be a Dihybrid ratio.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.880
Let us understand this interesting concept

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.420
in the next part!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.580
Here is a representative monohybrid cross

00:05:57.581 --> 00:06:00.539
on our screen which involves only one character

00:06:00.539 --> 00:06:01.039
at a time.

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:05.340
Do you think crossing a single character at

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.811
a time was enough for Mendel to arrive at

00:06:08.811 --> 00:06:10.589
concrete conclusions?

00:06:10.589 --> 00:06:12.180
Of course not!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.500
After all the seven pairs of contrasting characters

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.759
were crossed individually, Mendel went a step

00:06:18.759 --> 00:06:22.359
ahead and crossed plants considering two characters

00:06:22.359 --> 00:06:23.270
at a time.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.733
He tried the DIHYBRID cross .

00:06:25.733 --> 00:06:29.300
Let us take a simple example to understand

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.710
how the Dihybrid cross works!

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.719
Which two characters should we take now?

00:06:34.719 --> 00:06:37.653
We have already seen a monohybrid cross for

00:06:37.653 --> 00:06:40.860
characters like the plant height and the flower

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.930
colour individually.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:45.980
So let us consider these characters together

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.879
to understand the Dihybrid cross.

00:06:48.879 --> 00:06:51.890
For our convenience, we take one plant which

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.900
has both dominant characters while the other

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.300
with both having recessive characters.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.540
It means we take both the plants which are

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.280
HOMOZYGOUS . Any guesses about what the genotypes

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:05.849
will be?

00:07:05.849 --> 00:07:08.931
“TTPP” in upper case will be this plant

00:07:08.931 --> 00:07:12.409
which is tall, with purple coloured flowers.

00:07:12.409 --> 00:07:15.468
Similarly, “ttpp’’ in lower case will

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:19.189
represent a plant that is dwarf and has white

00:07:19.189 --> 00:07:20.270
coloured flowers.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:24.449
This is how we separate the gametes.

00:07:24.449 --> 00:07:28.509
Any idea why didn’t we write it as TT and PP?

00:07:28.509 --> 00:07:33.360
The alleles T and T represent the same trait.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.522
So they will have to be distributed in the

00:07:35.522 --> 00:07:36.500
respective gametes.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:40.330
They will not get together in the same cell.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.389
Similarly...

00:07:41.389 --> 00:07:43.897
P and P will get into the separate cells as

00:07:43.897 --> 00:07:46.580
they are the alleles for the same trait flower

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:47.580
colour!

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.319
It’s the same case in the other plant as well.

00:07:51.319 --> 00:07:53.360
This is how the gametes will be formed!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.629
Now we’re ready for the crossing!

00:07:56.629 --> 00:07:59.960
This is how the F1 generation would look.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.720
Take a moment to understand this!

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.976
Now to get a conclusive result, we need to

00:08:05.976 --> 00:08:09.309
cross the offsprings from the F1 generation

00:08:09.309 --> 00:08:11.770
and get the F2 generation.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:15.300
Let’s pick any two from the F one generation!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:19.529
Can you tell me how the gametes will be formed here?

00:08:19.529 --> 00:08:23.589
The gametes can be formed in these four different

00:08:23.589 --> 00:08:25.819
combinations for each case!

00:08:25.819 --> 00:08:27.979
Did you notice what happened?

00:08:27.979 --> 00:08:31.330
Will it be easy to do the crossing here?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.580
Definitely not!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.057
That is the reason why we opt for

00:08:35.057 --> 00:08:37.909
‘Punnett square’ for a Dihybrid cross.

00:08:37.909 --> 00:08:42.132
Let us get started with the cross for obtaining

00:08:42.132 --> 00:08:43.750
the F2 generation.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.459
We write the male and female symbols first.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.400
Followed by this, we write the respective

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.800
gametes here and here.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.800
And how do we cross these to fill in the 16 slots?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.320
We cross each row and column respectively.

00:08:59.329 --> 00:09:03.829
Here, this “TP” is crossed with this “TP”.

00:09:03.829 --> 00:09:06.509
So we obtain this slot.

00:09:06.509 --> 00:09:09.802
Similarly, we cross this “Tp” with “TP”

00:09:09.802 --> 00:09:11.660
to get this offspring.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.869
Can you try filling in the third and fourth

00:09:14.869 --> 00:09:16.810
slots in the first column?

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:20.990
We cross this “tP” with this “TP”

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:24.584
to obtain this offspring, and lastly, we cross

00:09:24.584 --> 00:09:27.240
this “tp” with this “TP” to obtain

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.300
this one!

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:32.437
All 4 as we can see in the table, are tall

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:34.529
with purple flowered plants.

00:09:34.529 --> 00:09:38.444
That’s because there is at least one capital

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:41.380
T and one capital P in each case!

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.839
If you wish to, you could pause the video

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:45.639
to fill in the other 12 slots.

00:09:45.639 --> 00:09:50.490
On similar lines, these are the results that

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.980
we obtain in the other slots!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.660
Take a moment to go through all of these!

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:01.670
Let’s count the different combinations now!

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:04.170
These are the four different possible combinations.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.339
‘Tall with purple flowered plants’, ‘tall

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:10.430
with white flowered plants’, ‘dwarf with

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.217
purple flowered plants’, and ‘dwarf with

00:10:13.217 --> 00:10:14.820
white flowered plants’.

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.807
Now can you count the number of plants that

00:10:17.807 --> 00:10:20.100
are tall and with purple flowers?

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.980
We have nine plants which are tall and with

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.259
purple coloured flowers.

00:10:25.259 --> 00:10:27.346
Can you count the number of plants for the

00:10:27.346 --> 00:10:28.389
other 3 combinations?

00:10:28.389 --> 00:10:32.730
Three plants show the tall trait along with

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.620
white flowers; and three show the dwarf trait

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.480
along with purple flowers.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.108
Six plants in all have mixed characters of

00:10:41.108 --> 00:10:43.480
the parents from the P1 generation.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:46.840
It means at least one recessive character

00:10:46.845 --> 00:10:49.100
is seen in these 6 plants.

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:52.023
Now, the last one among the sixteen shows

00:10:52.023 --> 00:10:55.089
both the recessive traits: a plant which is

00:10:55.089 --> 00:10:58.280
dwarf and has white flowers.

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:02.000
So if taken together, then we obtain a ratio

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:06.019
9 to 3 to 3 to 1 . This ratio is referred

00:11:06.019 --> 00:11:08.535
to as the Dihybrid Ratio .

00:11:08.535 --> 00:11:12.310
Nora has a simple question for you now!

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.580
Whenever any two characters are randomly taken

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:19.260
for a cross, do we obtain the same ratio?

00:11:19.269 --> 00:11:22.792
Say we take the seed colour and the seed shape

00:11:22.792 --> 00:11:25.089
will we obtain the same ratio?

00:11:25.089 --> 00:11:28.693
Well, if the cross is carried out correctly,

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.460
then we are bound to get ‘9 to 3 to 3 to

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:35.220
1’ as the Dihybrid ratio!

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.520
So if there are sixteen plants obtained in

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:41.620
the F2 generation, then 9 of them on an average

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:43.980
will express both the dominant characters.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:47.851
Like the tall height and purple coloured flowers

00:11:47.851 --> 00:11:48.900
in this case!

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:52.517
6 plants on an average will express a blend

00:11:52.517 --> 00:11:56.470
of both the characters: dominant and recessive.

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:59.221
Just like these 3 expressing tall height and

00:11:59.221 --> 00:12:02.160
white flowers, and these 3 showing dwarf height

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.279
and purple flowers!

00:12:04.279 --> 00:12:07.743
Lastly, only one out of the sixteen shows

00:12:07.743 --> 00:12:09.939
both recessive characters!

00:12:09.939 --> 00:12:14.110
Do you think we always get exactly 16 plants

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:16.100
in the F2 generation?

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.040
No not at all!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.567
There are numerous seeds obtained, which are

00:12:20.567 --> 00:12:22.980
then sown, and plants are grown to observe

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:25.160
these results!

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:28.100
Did Mendel get only 16 plants in the F2 generation?

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.490
This is also not the case!

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:33.810
Mendel had obtained many seeds.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.620
But when he grew plants from them, he obtained

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.980
the plants in certain numbers.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:42.060
When these numbers were calculated, the ratio

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:45.680
turned out to be 9 to 3 to 3 to 1.

00:12:45.689 --> 00:12:48.852
So basically, 9 to 3 to 3 to 1 is the RATIO

00:12:48.852 --> 00:12:51.500
obtained at the end of calculations!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:56.167
The total number of seeds and thus the plants

00:12:56.167 --> 00:12:59.279
obtained could be much higher.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:02.780
Do watch our videos based on Ratios if you

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.740
want to understand them better!

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:10.160
So 9 to 3 to 3 to 1 is the phenotypic ratio

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.040
for a Dihybrid cross!

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:15.592
Before we get deeper into Mendelian experiments,

00:13:15.592 --> 00:13:17.870
let us have a look at the laws put forth by

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.420
Mendel.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:22.180
Based on the observations of Monohybrid and

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:25.480
Dihybrid crosses, Mendel established three

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.639
extremely important LAWS in genetics.

00:13:27.639 --> 00:13:31.240
In the next part, let us have a look at them!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.161
Don’t forget to subscribe to our YouTube

00:13:34.161 --> 00:13:36.570
channel in order to get notified!

